ar Field Communication (NFC) technology for seamless transactions.\n\nApple Pay ensures the security of its users by not storing card numbers on devices or Apple servers. Instead, it uses a unique Device Account Number, encrypted and securely stored in the Secure Element on the user's device. This approach enhances privacy and security, as actual card details are never shared with merchants or transmitted during transactions.\n\nThe service is designed to work with iOS devices, allowing users to link their payment cards to the Apple Pay app installed on their iPhone or Apple Watch. This setup facilitates cashless transactions, making it a convenient option for users who prefer digital payments over traditional methods. Apple Pay's compatibility with various operating systems ensures that it is accessible to a wide range of users, further promoting the adoption of mobile payment solutions.\n\nOverall, Apple Pay represents a significant advancement in the realm of digital payments, offering a secure, efficient, and user-friendly alternative to conventional payment methods. Its introduction in Poland and other markets underscores its role in driving the adoption of contactless payment technologies worldwide.\",7\r\n44,GARMIN PAY,\"GARMIN PAY is a mobile payment system that has been available in Poland since March 2018. It allows users to make payments conveniently through their smartwatches. The service is supported by many banks in Poland, making it widely accessible to users who wish to utilize their Garmin smartwatches for contactless payments. This integration of technology and finance provides a seamless and efficient payment solution for those who prefer using wearable devices for their transactions.\",5\r\n45,FITBIT PAY,\"FITBIT PAY is a mobile payment system that was launched in October 2018. It is designed to cater to active individuals and athletes, providing them with a convenient and secure way to make payments on the go. The system is available through sel